# Beat Sheet

## Defend it
1. Premise / Why does it need to exists
What if someone was convinced trains weren't real

2. Who is in it
{{ VR = CLAIRE }} - A rational Woman who is married to a TRAIN DENIER. She gets angrier 
{{ VA = PHIL }} - A TRAIN DENIER. He becomes more nervous / maniac and more into eating his steak

3. Staging
I'm imagining they are eating on a train car. I think a cut to between the two of them. Maybe other patrons chime in asking if they could keep quiet.

4. What are the rules of the sketch
I think it’s pretty simple. {{VA}} says something like trains aren’t real {{VR}} says that obviously they are

5. Who is allowed to get laughs? Why are they allowed to get laughs? What is the treat of the sketch? [[Is the treat what we think it is? Maybe it’s what the “premise” is. We only want to hit that 3 times tops]]
{{VR}} is allowed to get laughs through comedic timing and grounding the scene. The treat is {{VA}} saying that trains are not real. The premise is a man driving his wife to murder through his weirdness
## The 5 w’s
Where you are

Who you are (in relationship to each other)

What you want

What is the problem?

What is the attempt at a solution? Murder
## Build up

We start off happy and then divulge into more angry and insane

===
## Beats

= ... I don’t know what that was. It was loud and had a horn
= a what stop?
=  That’s absurd they aren’t real
= *** The third time she says, "I can't believe I'm in love with a train denier"

= earthquake for 20 minutes
= fairies and pixies!  
= {{VA}}: this conversation is going off rails
= murder

===

INT. 
We see a happy couple enjoying their steaks, in a nice 

{{VR}}
Wow! I just wanted to say thank you honey for this dinner. It's been a while since we went out

{{VA}}
You're welcome! I've missed this

{{VR}}
I'm sorry I didn't mean to cut you off, you were saying

{{VA}}
Oh yeah! Something weird happened to me on the way home from work. I was just sitting around in traffic. 

{{VR}}
Mmhmm

{{VA}}
And then something passed in front of us. I don’t know what that was. It was loud and had a horn

{{VR}}
(takes a beat)
What?

{{VA}}
Yeah it was bizarre!

{{VR}}
(frustrated)
I think you were at a train stop

{{VA}}
(takes a beat incredulous)
A what stop?

{{VR}}
You know a train stop? You know a place where trains cross? With whistles and horns and they take an absurd amount of time to cross?

{{VA}}
nervous
Quit being absurd

{{VR}}
Nevermind. It's not worth arguing about

a pause passes between them

{{VR}}
I'm sorry I'm the one being absurd?

{{VA}}
Yeah you kind of are! Everyone knows trains aren't real

{{VR}}
Oh my god. I'm married to a train denier

{{VA}}
nervous
What? What? You genuinely believe that trains are real?

{{VR}}
Yes {{VA}} I am 100% convinced trains are indeed real

{{VA}}
No you are right it's not worth arguing about

{{VR}}
(pauses)
This steak is okay

{{VA}}
Yeah it's fine

pause

{{VR}}
The rumbling

{{VA}}
What?

{{VR}}
The one that been going on for the past 20 minutes

{{VA}}
It's just been a casual earthquake

{{VR}}
Really? There's been an earthquake going on for 20 minutes? 

{{VA}}
Yeah they happen all the time on our dinner dates

{{VR}}
We've been having dinner dates on... nevermind

{{VA}}
noticeable sweat
I need more water. 
